  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNIDAS II: Women&apos;s participation in peacebuilding,social cohesion,recov.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Venezuela&apos;s accentuated and sustained political polarization adds to the multiple global and national crises. Women&apos;s movements in Venezuela remain active and continue developing initiatives on women&#x2019;s rights and social cohesion. However the existing movements and organizations lack unity and full capacity to influence social and political high-level dialogues. 

The project seeks to adress and transform structural inequalities and gender violence through (1) greater incidence of women&apos;s rights advocates and peacebuilders in decision making for crisis recovery and (2) strengthened leadership in dialogue and peace building processes.</narrative>
  </description>
